1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,597
This is SecureOps Guardian, a human-controlled security investigation agent built in TrueForge.

2
00:00:04,597 --> 00:00:10,344
It is designed for security, platform, and on-call engineers who need to move from a

3
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:13,409
suspicious repository change to a reviewable, evidence-backed response.

4
00:00:13,409 --> 00:00:19,155
The left rail preserves sessions, the center holds the human conversation, and the investigation rail

5
00:00:19,155 --> 00:00:23,753
makes the execution visible instead of hiding it behind a final answer.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,542
One saved Guardian agent coordinates bounded specialist agents.

7
00:00:28,542 --> 00:00:31,642
Official GitHub MCP supplies real repository evidence.

8
00:00:31,642 --> 00:00:36,512
An owned Fixture MCP can contribute clearly labelled synthetic incident observations.

9
00:00:36,512 --> 00:00:40,940
Daytona provides an isolated sandbox for the pinned static verifier.

10
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:48,910
The human chooses the ceiling: read-only analysis, a verified proposal with no write, or an approval-gated pull request.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,734
The operator begins with the lowest capability.

12
00:00:52,734 --> 00:01:00,545
The request names the repository, base branch, suspect commit, and exact NetworkPolicy file, then explicitly forbids remediation and GitHub writes.

13
00:01:00,545 --> 00:01:03,669
Guardian compiles that natural-language request into bounded scope.

14
00:01:03,669 --> 00:01:09,528
While we fast-forward the model wait, the right rail shows the real progress: scope, evidence,

15
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:13,824
five GitHub MCP calls, zero sandbox steps, and zero write capability.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,455
The read-only run completes with high-severity finding SEC-NET-001.

17
00:01:19,455 --> 00:01:30,594
Guardian traces unrestricted egress to the exact commit and file: a zero-prefix CIDR now permits outbound IPv4 traffic from checkout-api.

18
00:01:30,594 --> 00:01:36,720
The result cites consumed GitHub evidence and keeps its limits explicit.

19
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:41,733
Repository facts do not prove deployment or live reachability.

20
00:01:41,733 --> 00:01:48,973
This run used no subagents, no Daytona sandbox, no approvals, and no writes.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,861
Now the human deliberately raises the capability.

22
00:01:52,861 --> 00:02:00,219
The follow-up asks Guardian to open a pull request, but only after checking that the proposed change works.

23
00:02:00,219 --> 00:02:03,081
This is not treated as blanket permission.

24
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:09,212
Changing from analysis to remediation creates a new run with a new scope decision, new

25
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:12,891
proof requirements, and separate control over any external write.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,941
Guardian presents the interpreted request before it proceeds: the exact repository, main branch, frozen revision,

27
00:02:22,941 --> 00:02:27,706
NetworkPolicy target, OPEN_PR mode, and the selected k8s-network-egress verifier.

28
00:02:27,706 --> 00:02:36,176
The card also states the ceiling: Fixture reads, Daytona verification, candidate generation, and approval-bound GitHub writes.

29
00:02:36,176 --> 00:02:38,823
The operator confirms this interpretation.

30
00:02:38,823 --> 00:02:44,117
Guardian still cannot merge, deploy, or access a live cluster.

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,296
TrueForge spawns two bounded specialists.

32
00:02:47,296 --> 00:02:55,564
The Change Security Investigator uses official GitHub evidence to reconstruct the change and identify the unrestricted egress rule.

33
00:02:55,564 --> 00:03:02,453
The Exposure Evidence Investigator makes four calls to the owned Fixture MCP: security alert, deployment

34
00:03:02,453 --> 00:03:05,209
observation, reachability observation, and service dependencies.

35
00:03:05,209 --> 00:03:13,476
The recording lets us click into each agent and inspect findings, evidence references, activity, call counts, and duration.

36
00:03:13,476 --> 00:03:16,691
Real and synthetic sources remain clearly separated.

37
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,413
The evidence is joined only after both specialists complete.

38
00:03:29,413 --> 00:03:31,374
GitHub establishes what changed.

39
00:03:31,374 --> 00:03:37,258
The synthetic fixture reports that checkout-api reached the declared forbidden test destination.

40
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:44,123
Guardian records the exact evidence identifiers and preserves unknowns instead of overstating runtime truth.

41
00:03:44,123 --> 00:03:51,478
The overview now shows two completed agents, ten MCP calls, their individual steps, and a

42
00:03:51,478 --> 00:03:55,891
persistent execution trace that a reviewer can reopen later.

43
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,335
Next, the proposed NetworkPolicy change runs inside the Daytona sandbox with a pinned verifier.

44
00:04:05,335 --> 00:04:11,052
Six sandbox steps evaluate a four-state matrix: last-known-good is secure and functional, the suspect state

45
00:04:11,052 --> 00:04:17,530
is exposed, deny-all is secure but operationally rejected, and the Guardian candidate is both secure and functional.

46
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:24,009
The proposal hash and verified candidate identity bind the later write to exactly what passed this proof.

47
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,706
Before GitHub changes, Guardian rechecks branches, existing pull requests, file contents, and commits.

48
00:04:29,706 --> 00:04:32,965
The create-pull-request action stops at a visible human-in-the-loop gate.

49
00:04:32,965 --> 00:04:38,033
Only after the operator approves does the official GitHub MCP perform the controlled write.

50
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:45,274
The terminal receipt records one write, one approval, the completed agents, six sandbox steps, eight GitHub MCP steps, and PR_CREATED.

51
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:52,062
The result is a real, reviewable pull request carrying the proposal hash, verified candidate identity, verifier version, and four-state proof.

52
00:04:52,062 --> 00:04:56,458
Guardian investigated with evidence, verified in Daytona, and wrote only after human approval.

53
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:59,501
It leaves the final merge to the accountable reviewer.
